# What the image build must not see.
#
# This is also the list the Docker workflow uses to decide whether a push has
# anything to build (.github/scripts/deploy-scope): a push that changes only
# paths excluded here builds nothing. So an entry must be something the image
# really does not need. Write plain root paths, one per line; a glob still
# keeps files out of the build but is not used for skipping.

# Local build output and state.
herald
herald-web
herald.db*
.git
.omc
.claude

# Docs, plans and repo guidance.
docs
plans
CHANGELOG.md
CLAUDE.md
INSTALL.md
PROJECT_STATUS.md
QUICKSTART.md
README.md
SECURITY.md
USAGE.md
LICENSE

# CI, dev tooling and host-install files. None of it is compiled in.
.github
.vscode
githooks
systemd
.editorconfig
.envrc
.gitignore
.golangci.yml
.goreleaser.yml
Makefile
Taskfile.yml
docker-compose.yml
sqlc.yaml
test_feeds.opml
